MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT — AGRISHIELD

Complete Farmer-Centric AI Platform: UI/UX, Backend, Machine Learning, Market Intelligence, Security and Deployment

1. Your Role

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, UI/UX designer, machine-learning engineer, data engineer, agricultural technology specialist, security engineer and QA tester.

Your task is to inspect, improve, test and complete my existing AgriShield project. Do not stop after creating a visually attractive dashboard. Deliver a working, integrated application with reliable data handling, usable farmer workflows, useful administration tools, explainable ML predictions and clear documentation.

Project name: AgriShield

Full title: AgriShield — AI-Powered Crop Market Intelligence, Pre-Sowing Advisory and Post-Harvest Rescue System

Primary users: Indian farmers, especially small and marginal farmers, and authorized administrators.

Technology direction: Python Flask backend, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, Bootstrap where appropriate, SQLite for local development, pandas, scikit-learn and joblib for ML, with optional external market-data integrations.

Important constraints:

- Work with the existing project and preserve useful functionality.
- Keep the application affordable to run and suitable for a college project demonstration.
- Do not require paid APIs, cloud accounts, payment cards or proprietary services for core local functionality.
- Use real data when verified sources are configured; clearly identify demo data otherwise.
- Do not fabricate market prices, model predictions, farmer records, API success or evaluation metrics.
- Do not claim that AgriShield guarantees profits, prevents losses or replaces agricultural experts.

